One design issue surfaced before the oracle evidence could be obtained: a cubic’s depressed form makes the intended symmetry nearly automatic, so increasing \(p\) mostly adds arithmetic rather than structural discovery. I’m strengthening the same paper-native family to \(h=11\): the witness remains short (11 linear factors), Section 3 applies unchanged, and centering still gives a compact two-coefficient invariant, but a generic solver now faces genuine degree-11 finite-field factorization. This keeps the answer fixed-length while widening the mechanical/compact gap.
