codex
The replacement module passes its own gates, but its first measurements reveal a real H/G9 problem: the “compact” moment route costs up to 279 operations, while the standard correspondence search is only a few hundred candidate checks because the multiplier congruence filters aggressively. I’m correcting that rather than accepting a nominal pass: precompute exact moment checksums as instance data, enlarge the shipping sets at fixed two-integer answer length, and remeasure the honest compression gap.
