Implemented a native Track B affine-equivalence generator based on Theorem 3 and Section 3 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.12406).

Local verification succeeded:

- Planted witnesses: 16/16
- Random guesses: 0/200,000
- Exact answer density: 1 in 4,933,621,440
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each
- Reference algorithm: about 6,004 operations per instance
- Compact invariant route: at most 256 operations
- Answer size: 13 characters, 2 atoms

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.12406/gen_2308_12406.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.12406/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.12406/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2308.12406/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
